      "content": "[{\"id\":4825806524,\"body\":\"### Servicing repro — `Math.Round(2.5)` midpoint rounding\\n\\n**Issue.** `Math.Round(double)` uses banker's rounding (`MidpointRounding.ToEven`) by default, so `Math.Round(2.5)` returns `2` instead of `3`. Customers porting from frameworks that round half away from zero get incorrect totals.\\n\\n**Repro approach.** Minimal **csproj console app** targeting `net9.0`. (The preferred xunit unit test can't restore packages offline in this environment, and a file-based `dotnet run app.cs` repro requires a .NET 10+ SDK.) Built and run on the **baseline GA .NET 9 SDK `9.0.315`** (runtime `9.0.17`), which still exhibits the bug.\\n\\n**Isolating call site** (`repro/Program.cs`):\\n\\n```csharp\\ndouble input = 2.5;\\ndouble expected = 3;                 // PR Expected Result: Math.Round(2.5) == 3\\ndouble actual = Math.Round(input);   // isolated call site under test\\n\\nif (actual != expected)\\n    Console.WriteLine($\\\"REPRO CONFIRMED: Math.Round({input}) returned {actual}, expected {expected}.\\\");\\n```\\n\\n**Expected Result.** `Math.Round(2.5)` returns `3`.\\n\\n**Actual Result** (quoted from the captured `output.log`):\\n\\n```\\n=== dotnet run ===\\nCall:     Math.Round(2.5)\\nExpected: 3\\nActual:   2\\nREPRO CONFIRMED: Math.Round(2.5) returned 2, expected 3.\\nexit=1\\n```\\n\\nThe bug **reproduces**: `Math.Round(2.5)` yields `2` on the baseline GA .NET 9 SDK instead of the expected `3`.\\n\\n**Artifact.** The repro sources + `output.log` are uploaded as artifact **`servicing-repro-pr-1`** on this workflow run: https://github.com/jeffhandley/dotnet-runtime-servicing-release-manager/actions/runs/28318977468\\n\\n\\n\\n> Generated by [Servicing Repro Producer](https://github.com/jeffhandley/dotnet-runtime-servicing-release-manager/actions/runs/28318977468) · 251.1 AIC · ⊞ 6.8K · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Ajeffhandley%2Fdotnet-runtime-servicing-release-manager+%22gh-aw-workflow-call-id%3A+jeffhandley%2